## Delivered

- The exact six firm-scoped accountant routes and six identifier-free client
  routes map over the T02 workflow contracts. Firm and client scope remain
  server-derived and are revalidated on every operation.
- Read-only link confirmation exchanges a protected digest proof for one secure,
  HTTP-only, SameSite-Strict, path-scoped protected session cookie and redirects
  to a clean URL.
- Public, session, answer, upload, and submission limits run before resource
  validity and return fixed non-oracular responses with the shared intake
  browser-header policy.
- Every successful screen is a strongly typed presentation-only Razor
  component. Review and accountant screens stay static SSR; only the closed-code
  questionnaire reveal panel uses Interactive Server, with detailed errors and
  WebSocket compression disabled.
- The local upload module sends only `upload.bin` and the antiforgery header.
  `MultipartReader` streams one configured file, discards the received filename,
  preserves zero-byte input for backend rejection/audit, and rejects a second
  section before a valid workflow can complete.
- Accountant progress renders the backend projection, never recovers a raw
  client URL, and links to the unchanged review route only after verified ready
  association.

## Boundary retained

No production file under ClientIntake, Persistence, Tenancy, TaxCases,
CaseReview, CaseProcessing, DocumentExtraction, or TaxLogicEngine changed. No
migration, model snapshot, schema shape, review contract, raw-content read or
download path, extraction, tax processing, review manufacture, production
content provider, retention rule, or deployment authorization was added.

The encrypted opaque source object outside web root remains the sole
potentially SIN-bearing exception. T03 verifies the HTTP/component layer with
controlled collaborators; T04 still owns final cross-module AC-1 through AC-99
verification and the spec-completion claim.

